Crossed box, orientations A and B, 3 kinematic points x 4 gluon helicities x 9 Z polarisations,
generic loop momenta and loop momenta collinear to p1:
   v^2 Z couplings              expected B/A = +1
   a^2 Z couplings              expected B/A = +1
   v a cross terms              expected B/A = -1
   scalar (Yukawa) vertices     expected B/A = +1
largest deviation of B/A from the expected value: 3.2e-10
So the full amplitude contains the crossed box twice for the v^2 + a^2 and scalar parts:
a coefficient extracted from the full gg -> ZZ or gg -> HH amplitude is 2 x the single-box value.
